    <p>Control Node: WSL (Ubuntu)</p>

    <p>Managed Node: AWS EC2</p>

    <p>I am learning Ansible through hands-on practice.</p>
</body>
</html>

## 8. Running the Playbook

I ran the playbook using:

ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini first-playbook.yaml --limit app_key

The `--limit app_key` option tells Ansible to run the playbook only on hosts in the `app_key` group.

## 9. Playbook Result

The playbook completed successfully.

ec2-1 : ok=3 changed=2 unreachable=0 failed=0

### What the result means

`ok=3`

Three tasks completed successfully, including fact gathering.

`changed=2`

Two tasks made changes on the EC2 server:

* Apache was installed
* `index.html` was copied

`unreachable=0`

Ansible successfully connected to the EC2 server.

`failed=0`

No task failed.

## 10. AWS Security Group

After deploying Apache, I allowed HTTP traffic through the EC2 Security Group.

Type       : HTTP
Protocol   : TCP
Port       : 80

This allowed the web browser to access Apache running on the EC2 instance.

## 11. Verify the Web Server

I opened the EC2 public IP in my browser:

http://EC2-PUBLIC-IP

The custom HTML page was displayed successfully.

This confirmed that:

Ansible
   ↓
Connected to EC2
   ↓
Installed Apache
   ↓
Copied index.html
   ↓
Apache served the page
   ↓
Browser displayed the webpage

